  "body": "Part 2 of 2 for #3098. This change adds a Camcraft Klartext post for a Fehlmann Picomax 55 with an iTNC 530 and NC software `340490-03`. The Picomax machine definition offers this post. Existing Heidenhain DIN/ISO configurations retain their post.\n\nThe writer accepts one metric setup, a stock box, one preset, XYZ straight moves, plunges and constant-height XY arcs. It supports the stated manual tool-change procedure and flood coolant. It refuses an unknown release, an unsupported operation, an incompatible tool or conflicting definitions of a tool number. Refusals stop the save and preserve an existing NC file.\n\n### Station results\n\nThe public CLI produced the following files. A byte comparison matched each file to the original input for the HEIDENHAIN iTNC 530 programming station, NC software `606425 004 SP20`.\n\n| Sample | Blocks | Programmed stops reached | Test Run result |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Single-tool XY arc contour | 41 | 3 of 3 | Program end |\n| Two-tool contour with flood coolant | 63 | 5 of 5 | Program end |\n\nBoth files passed the controller converter's round trip with zero normalized block differences. Neither run logged an NC error. Configuring the station's release as a post target still gives a refusal. Qualification of a release requires separate evidence for the full supported scope.\n\n### Checks on the target machine\n\nThe target manual describes the active travel limit for `M140 MB MAX` in §7.4, p. 303. Cycle 247 does not activate the preset in Test Run (§8.9, p. 492). On the physical Picomax, check the populated XYZ preset and coordinate state, tool and holder clearance, quill and drive state, tool table and coolant. The machine definition gives rapid rates. The installation's cutting-feed ceiling and machine-coordinate travel limits remain open. [HEIDENHAIN iTNC 530 manual for 340 49x-03](https://content.heidenhain.de/doku/tnc_guide/pdf_files/iTNC530/34049x-neu/en/bhb.pdf)\n\n### Verification\n\nThe post revision `5081fd8f6` includes the machine definition at `e6e04f5d0`. The quick gate passed 385 steps and recorded 3,009 test passes. The heavy gate passed 199 steps and recorded 43 release test passes. Strict Clippy passed for all targets in the app and post crates.\n\nThe public app and CLI tests cover the supported contour, disk output, project reopening, and refusal before overwriting a file. The two station inputs were 1,081 and 1,597 bytes. A separate 3,627-byte app program also matched its reference. Configuring either `340490-04` or `606425-04` produced a diagnostic, left a new destination absent, and preserved an existing file. The comment tests cover executable-block integrity across all 20 posts.\n\nPriority: P4, as on #3182.\n\nChangelog: A new Klartext post writes single-setup metric XYZ milling programs for the Fehlmann Picomax 55 with iTNC 530 NC software 340490-03.\n\nRefs #3204\nRefs #3098\n\nFixes #3182\n",
